│     FastAPI now unwraps decorated dependencies (such as `functools.cache`) before deciding whether they are coroutines or generators, so a     │
│ cached async dependency is awaited instead of being returned as a raw coroutine. The fix is in `fastapi/dependencies/models.py`: the three     │
│ checks (`is_gen_callable`, `is_async_gen_callable`, `is_coroutine_callable`) now inspect `inspect.unwrap(self.call)`. The issue's `@cache`     │
│ example returns `'ok'` through `TestClient`, and the dependency cache, class dependency and after-yield tests pass. I did not add a test for   │
│ the wrapped-dependency case.                                                                                                                   │
